cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "cyberdef-vuln: a QLoRA study of defensive vulnerability detection with small open models"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Pallav
    family-names: Pokhriyal
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5356-7663"
    email: pallav01@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pallav0107/cyberdef-llm"
keywords:
  - vulnerability detection
  - secure code review
  - large language models
  - QLoRA
  - defensive security
abstract: >
  A reproducible study of whether QLoRA fine-tuning of a small open instruct model
  (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) yields transferable code-vulnerability-detection skill, evaluated
  under an identical prompt on the recognized CodeXGLUE Defect Detection (Devign)
  benchmark, with explicit leakage controls and automatic recomputation of all reported
  scores. Includes honest negative results.
